  "notes": "USAGE:\n{排水|はいすい} can refer to both the act of draining water and the drained water itself. It is used in everyday contexts (household plumbing) as well as environmental and industrial contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {排水|はいすい}{口|こう} (drain outlet, drain hole)\n- {排水|はいすい}{管|かん} (drainage pipe)\n- {排水|はいすい}{溝|こう} (drainage ditch/gutter)\n- {排水|はいすい}{処理|しょり} (wastewater treatment)\n- {排水|はいすい}{基準|きじゅん} (wastewater standards)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {給水|きゅうすい} (water supply — the opposite process)\n- {下水|げすい} (sewage, sewerage)\n- {排水|はいすい}トラップ (drain trap — the U-shaped pipe under sinks)",
